<title>TURKEY: TABLE-TURK AKBANK H1 NET PROFIT RISES.</title>
<headline>TABLE-TURK AKBANK H1 NET PROFIT RISES.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-June 1997 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>					 H1 1997	   H1 1996</p>
<p>					 -------	   -------</p>
<p>    Per share profit		 820.25  vs     805.42</p>
<p>    Net Profit		    41,012.36  vs  14,497.62</p>
<p>    Net interest income	 78,168.50  vs  27,385.12</p>
<p>    Net non-interest expense  19,647.44  vs   7,001.52</p>
<p>    Provisions for bad loans     435.50  vs	79.68</p>
<p>    Deposits		     465,293.60  vs 224,127.16</p>
<p>    Loans borrowed		10,585.92  vs   2,162.01</p>
<p>    Loans extended	     246,589.44  vs  81,211.83</p>
<p>    Equity			  85,774.43  vs  37,230.96</p>
<p>    Capital			 50,000.00  vs  18,000.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Akbank T.A.S is one of Turkey's leading commercial banks, owned largely by industrial conglomerate Sabancg Holding.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 78 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in June.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212 275 08 75</p>
</text>
